# Millrace Standards

- Apply SOLID, DRY, and YAGNI. Prefer small modules with explicit interfaces.
- Keep Python fully typed. Enforce Ruff and strict Pyright checks.
- Remove unused imports, dead code, placeholders, and speculative abstractions.
- Write concise comments only when they explain a non-obvious decision.
- Use deterministic, idempotent data operations and fail closed on validation errors.
- Keep configuration externalized and validate it at process boundaries.
- Never expose secrets or place credentials in tracked files.
- Do not mention generated assistance in source, documentation, commits, or review text.
- Do not use em dashes.
- Use concise, imperative commit subjects when commits are explicitly requested.
